  "result": "The cause is in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py:603`). It builds the `shlex` lexer directly, so the default comment character `#` stays active. Everything after a `#` is dropped, for example `cli a#b c` becomes `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`. That shifts the argument and cursor indexes, which gives the wrong completions. Fish can also hit an `IndexError` in the same situation.\n\nI've written the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-sleepy-dove.md`. I'm in plan mode, so nothing has been edited yet.\n\n**Planned changes**\n1. In `src/click/shell_completion.py`, add `lex.commenters = \"\"` right after `lex.whitespace_split = True`. This is what `shlex.split` does internally.\n2. In `tests/test_parser.py`, add cases to `test_split_arg_string`:\n   - `\"cli #foo bar\"` \u2192 `[\"cli\", \"#foo\", \"bar\"]`\n   - `\"cli a#b c\"` \u2192 `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]`\n   - `\"cli '#a' b\"` \u2192 `[\"cli\", \"#a\", \"b\"]`\n3. Add a bugfix entry to `CHANGES.rst`.\n\n**Verification:** run `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py`, and confirm the new cases fail before the fix and pass after.\n\nI couldn't load the plan-approval tool in this session, so please confirm here if you'd like me to go ahead and apply the fix.",
